================================================================================
3. BEND MATH — VERIFIED AGAINST FUSION 360
================================================================================

All formulas for 90-degree air bending:

  OSS = R + T                          Outside Setback (= tan(45°) × (R+T))
  BA  = (π/2) × (R + K × T)           Bend Allowance
  BD  = 2 × OSS - BA = 2(R+T) - BA    Bend Deduction
  BA/2 = (π/4) × (R + K × T)          Bend CL offset from hard corner

Verified values (0.1875" 3003, R=0.125, K=0.33):
  OSS  = 0.3125"
  BA   = 0.2935"   [Fusion measures 0.294" bend zone ✓]
  BD   = 0.3315"
  BA/2 = 0.1468"   [Fusion: 0.147" ✓]

Flat zone formulas:
  f2 = nominal_f2 - BD/2        lip zone (blank edge to bend2 CL)
     = 2.25 - 0.166 = 2.084"    [Fusion: 2.084" ✓]

  f1 = nominal_f1 - 3×BD/2      leg zone (used for blank SIZE only)
     = 2.00 - 0.497 = 1.503"

  CL-to-CL span = nominal_f1 - BD = 2.00 - 0.331 = 1.669"  [Fusion: 1.669" ✓]

  ex = f1 + f2 = 3.587" per side

Blank size:
  blank_w = face_width  + 2 × ex = 24 + 7.174 = 31.174"  [Fusion: 31.174" ✓]
  blank_h = face_height + 2 × ex = 36 + 7.174 = 43.174"  [Fusion: 43.174" ✓]

Hard corner placement:
  HC_offset = ex + BD = 3.587 + 0.331 = 3.918" from blank edge
  HC-HC_w = 31.174 - 2×3.918 = 23.338"  [Fusion: 23.36" ✓]
  HC-HC_h = 43.174 - 2×3.918 = 35.338"  [Fusion: 35.367" ✓]

Layout from blank edge inward:
  [blank edge]--f2=2.084"--[bend2 CL]--1.669"--[bend1 CL]--BA/2=0.147"--[HC]--face

Bend line positions:
  bend2 CL from blank edge = f2 = 2.084"          [Fusion: 2.084" ✓]
  bend1 CL from blank edge = HC - BA/2 = 3.771"
  bend1 CL from HC         = BA/2 = 0.147"         [Fusion: 0.147" ✓]
  bend2 CL from HC         = HC - f2 = 1.834"      [Fusion: 1.823" ✓]

PHYSICAL DESCRIPTION:
  Bend 1 = leg fold, tight to face (small BA/2 offset)
  Bend 2 = J return lip fold (the return that forms the J channel)
  Flange1 folds 90° AWAY from face, flange2 folds 90° BACK toward face.

All differences from Fusion < 0.015" = accumulated rounding, within fab tolerance.


================================================================================
4. FLAT PATTERN GEOMETRY — VARIABLE-EDGE OUTLINE
================================================================================

The blank outline is a variable-sided closed polygon. Edge count depends on the
flange configuration at each of the 4 corners.

CORNER TYPES:
  Type A (J+J): 4 edges — void_edge, miter, miter, void_edge
  Type B (L+L): 2 edges — notch_wall, notch_wall (reach blank edge directly)
  Type C (J+L): 3 edges — void_edge, miter, notch_wall
  Type D (J+N): 2 edges — void_edge, miter (inactive side = square face end)
  Type E (L+N): 1 edge  — notch_wall only
  Type F (N+N): 0 edges — point only

EDGE COUNTS BY FLANGE CODE:
  J4S           4 A-corners × 4 + 4 primary = 20 edges
  L4S           4 B-corners × 2 + 4 primary = 12 edges
  J2TB          4 D-corners × 2 + 4 primary = 12 edges
  L2TB          4 E-corners × 1 + 4 primary =  8 edges
  J2LR          4 D-corners × 2 + 4 primary = 12 edges
  L2LR          4 E-corners × 1 + 4 primary =  8 edges
  MIX J-tb/L-lr 4 C-corners × 3 + 4 primary = 16 edges

KEY GEOMETRY RULES:
  void_edge_length = f1 + BD
    This ensures the miter starts EXACTLY at the bend2 centerline.
    Prevents miter from cutting into the f1 leg zone.

  For L flanges: f2=0, so void_end reaches blank edge directly (no miter step).

  Miter: 45° diagonal, length = √2 × f2 = √2 × 2.084 = 2.948" ✓
  Miter starts at bend2 CL level, ends on blank outer edge.
  Purpose: allows flange2 (lip) to fold back without adjacent lips colliding.

J4S REFERENCE OUTLINE (20 points, CCW, blank coords with 0,0 at BL blank corner):
   1: (fx0-vl,  fy0)       BL close miter end / left primary end
   2: (fx0,     fy0)       BL hard corner (void inner, 90° inside corner)
   3: (fx0,     fy0-vb)    BL void edge down (ends at bend2 CL level)
   4: (fx0+mb,  0)         BL miter end = bottom primary start
   5: (fx1-mb,  0)         bottom primary end
   6: (fx1,     fy0-vb)    BR miter end
   7: (fx1,     fy0)       BR hard corner
   8: (fx1+vr,  fy0)       BR void edge right
   9: (bw,      fy0+mr)    BR miter end = right primary start
  10: (bw,      fy1-mr)    right primary end
  11: (fx1+vr,  fy1)       TR miter end
  12: (fx1,     fy1)       TR hard corner
  13: (fx1,     fy1+vt)    TR void edge up
  14: (fx1-mt,  bh)        TR miter end = top primary start
  15: (fx0+mt,  bh)        top primary end
  16: (fx0,     fy1+vt)    TL miter end
  17: (fx0,     fy1)       TL hard corner
  18: (fx0-vl,  fy1)       TL void edge left
  19: (0,       fy1-ml)    TL miter end = left primary start
  20: (0,       fy0+ml)    left primary end

Where:
  fx0 = el+BD,   fy0 = eb+BD    (BL hard corner)
  fx1 = bw-er-BD, fy1 = bh-et-BD (TR hard corner)
  vb/vt/vl/vr = f1+BD per side  (void edge lengths)
  mb/mt/ml/mr = f2 per side     (miter depths, 0 for L flanges)
  el/er/eb/et = f1+f2 per side  (blank extensions)


================================================================================
5. DXF LAYERS
================================================================================

  Layer       Color  Content
  ----------  -----  ----------------------------------------------------------
  cut         1      Blank outline polygon (variable sides per flange config)
  bend        3      Bend 1 and Bend 2 centerlines (individual line segments)
  holes       2      Perforation circles
  fastening   5      Fastener holes

No bend_extent layer (removed).

Bend line rules:
  Bend 1 CL (leg): BA/2 outward from each hard corner — 4 line segments
  Bend 2 CL (lip, J only): f2 inward from blank edge — 4 line segments
  All bend lines span hard-corner-to-hard-corner width/height only
  (not across full blank width — they stop at the face zone boundaries)


================================================================================
6. DATA MODEL
================================================================================

PanelSpec fields:
  panel_id           str    Output filename (no extension)
  face_width         float  Nominal face width (inches)
  face_height        float  Nominal face height (inches)
  thickness          float  Material thickness (inches) or gauge string
  flange_code        str    L4S / J4S / L2TB / J2TB / L2LR / J2LR / MIX
  flange_type        str    L or J (derived from flange_code)
  flange1_depth      float  Nominal leg depth (tight to face, Bend 1)
  flange2_depth      float  Nominal lip depth (J return, Bend 2), None for L
  hole_dia           float  Perforation diameter
  pitch              float  Hole center-to-center spacing
  pattern            str    straight or staggered
  fastening_pair     str    all/standard/tb/lr/t/b/l/r/none
  fastener_dia       float  Fastener hole diameter (default 0.1875")
  material           str    aluminum or steel
  alloy              str    3003 / 5052 / 6061 / steel
  k_factor_override  float  Optional per-panel K-factor override
  bend_radius_override float Optional per-panel bend radius override
  gap_override       float  Optional bend zone gap override
  stagger_angle      float  Stagger angle in degrees (default 60°)
  margin             float  Perforation clearance from hard corner (default 1.25")
  top/bottom/left/right_type  str   MIX mode: L or J per side
  top/bottom/left/right_f1    float MIX mode: nominal leg depth per side
  top/bottom/left/right_f2    float MIX mode: nominal lip depth per side

SideDef fields (computed by resolve_sides()):
  active  bool   Whether this side has a flange
  ftype   str    L or J
  f1      float  Flat leg length (blank sizing: nominal - 3×BD/2 for J, - BD/2 for L)
  f2      float  Flat lip length (nominal - BD/2, J only; 0 for L)


================================================================================
7. FLANGE CODES
================================================================================

  L4S   L flange all 4 sides, same depth
  J4S   J flange all 4 sides, same depth
  L2TB  L flange top + bottom only (left/right inactive)
  J2TB  J flange top + bottom only (left/right inactive)
  L2LR  L flange left + right only (top/bottom inactive)
  J2LR  J flange left + right only (top/bottom inactive)
  MIX   Per-side type and depth via CSV *_type/*_f1/*_f2 columns

Single letters L and J are normalized to L4S and J4S.


================================================================================
8. KEY FUNCTIONS
================================================================================

  get_rules(spec)
    Returns {r, k} — bend radius and K-factor for this spec
    r = 2/3 × t (current rule, pending full material table)
    k = K_FACTORS.get(alloy, K_DEFAULT)

  _bd(r, k, t)          Full bend deduction for 90-degree bend
  _ba_half(r, k, t)     BA/2 = bend CL offset from hard corner
  _flat_lip(nom, r,k,t) f2 = nominal - BD/2
  _flat_leg_J(nom,r,k,t) f1 = nominal - 3×BD/2  (for blank sizing)
  _flat_leg_L(nom,r,k,t) f1 = nominal - BD/2
  resolve_sides(spec)   Returns dict of SideDef per side (top/bottom/left/right)
  _side_extra(sd)       f1+f2 per side — used for blank extension calculation
  flat_size(spec)       Returns (blank_w, blank_h)

  _blank_outline(bw, bh, sides, bd)
    Returns CCW polygon point list (variable length by flange config)
    Uses _corner() internally for per-corner geometry
    Corner function: _corner(hsd, vsd, hc_x, hc_y, ox, oy)

  _draw_bend_lines(msp, fx0, fy0, fx1, fy1, blank_w, blank_h, sides, ba2)
    Draws Bend 1 and Bend 2 centerlines on bend layer

  _hole_centers(face_x, face_y, face_w, face_h, hole_dia, pitch, pattern,
                stagger_angle, margin)
    Returns list of (x, y) perforation centers

  _draw_fastening_holes(msp, spec, fx0, fy0, fx1, fy1, face_w, face_h,
                         sides, blank_w, blank_h)
    Draws fastening holes on fastening layer

  generate_panel_dxf(spec, outdir)
    Main entry point. Creates DXF and saves to outdir/panel_id.dxf

  parse_csv(path)
    Parses CSV file, returns list[PanelSpec]
    Normalizes headers (lowercase, strip whitespace)
    Supports gauge strings: "16 ga"=0.0625, "14 ga"=0.0800, "11 ga"=0.1250

  nest_panels(panels, sw, sh)   Stub — returns [] (nesting not implemented)
  write_nesting_dxf(sheets, outdir)  Stub — returns None


================================================================================
9. CSV FORMAT
================================================================================

Required: panel_id, width, height, thickness, flange_code, flange1_depth,
          hole_diameter, hole_pitch, pattern

Optional: flange2_depth, fastening_pair, fastener_dia, alloy, material,
          k_factor_override, bend_radius_override, gap_override,
          stagger_angle, margin

MIX columns: top_type, top_f1, top_f2, bottom_type, bottom_f1, bottom_f2,
             left_type, left_f1, left_f2, right_type, right_f1, right_f2

Thickness: decimal inches (0.0625, 0.080, 0.125, 0.1875, 0.250)
           or gauge string ("16 ga", "14 ga", "11 ga")
Pattern: straight or staggered
Fastening_pair: all, standard, tb, lr, t, b, l, r, none
Flange_code: L4S, J4S, L2TB, J2TB, L2LR, J2LR, MIX (or single L/J)


================================================================================
10. PERFORATION PATTERNS
================================================================================

Straight: rows and columns aligned, spacing = pitch in both x and y.

Staggered: every other row offset by pitch × cos(stagger_angle).
  Row-to-row step = pitch × sin(stagger_angle). Default angle = 60°.

Perforations placed within hard-corner-to-hard-corner face zone with
margin clearance on all sides.


================================================================================
11. FASTENING HOLES
================================================================================

J flanges: holes in lip zone (f2 area), centered at f2/2 from blank edge.
  Positions aligned to face perforation grid rows/columns at ~12" o.c.
  starting from first available perforation position.

L flanges: holes in leg zone (f1 area), centered at f1/2 from hard corner.
  2" margins at each end, equal spacing at ~12" o.c.

fastening_pair values:
  all / standard  all active sides
  tb              top + bottom only
  lr              left + right only
  t / b / l / r   single side
  none            no fastening holes


